From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:20:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3576-generic: enable preboot for the reboot modes

setup_boot_mode() turns the BOOT_LOADER and BOOT_UMS reboot flags into a
"preboot" command that starts the rockusb or ums gadget on the eMMC. But
main_loop() runs preboot only when CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT is set, and
generic-rk3576_defconfig leaves it unset. So "reboot loader" and
"reboot ums" from Linux arm a command that never runs, and the board
boots normally instead of entering USB flash mode.

Enable USE_PREBOOT. PREBOOT stays empty, so a normal boot runs nothing
extra; setup_boot_mode() fills it only for the one boot after a reboot
that asks for a gadget, and the armed command deletes the variable as
its first step.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 configs/generic-rk3576_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/generic-rk3576_defconfig b/configs/generic-rk3576_defconfig
index 5e256538..0e228e7e 100644
--- a/configs/generic-rk3576_defconfig
+++ b/configs/generic-rk3576_defconfig
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_BASE=0x2AD40000
 CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_CLOCK=24000000
 CONFIG_DEBUG_UART=y
 # CONFIG_BOOTMETH_VBE is not set
+CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE="rockchip/rk3576-generic.dtb"
 # CONFIG_DISPLAY_CPUINFO is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0x40000
-- 
